        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Process Identifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763970263680"
          },
          "code": "PROCESS_IDENTIFIER",
          "id": "1763969703051",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763969703053_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Take this as input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nFrom this response you will have to identify either the process name, action and if action is async or not. \n\nCase 1: Process name\nFrom this response identify the process name. Use following instructions to do it\n• From the user’s message, extract only the process name. \n• For example, if the input is “Enable bypass for promote”, extract promote as the process name and Enable bypass as action. \n• If user input specifically states to set async bypass then set isAsyncThere to true otherwise set it false. \n\nThese are the valid actions that you have to match from user input\n1. Enable bypass \n2. Disable bypass\n3. Update\n\nOutput action should follow this style \n1. enableBypass\n2. disableBypass\n3. update\n\nExamples - \n• Input: “Update approvalDisabled flag for Onboarding” \n• Output: {\"processName\":\"Onboarding\",\"action\":\"update\",\"isAsyncThere\":false}\n\n• Input: \"Enable async bypass for promote\"\n• Output: {\"processName\":\"Promote\",\"action\":\"enableBypass\",\"isAsyncThere\":true}\n\n• Input: \"Enable bypass for Change Personal Information\"\n• Output: {\"processName\":\"Change Personal Information\",\"action\":\"enable bypass\",\"isAsyncThere\":false}\n\n• Input: \"Disable bypass for Transfer\"\n• Output: {\"processName\":\"Transfer\",\"action\":\"disableBypass\",\"isAsyncThere\":false}\n\n• Input: \"Enable bypass for Approve Development Goal: Goal Share Action\"\n• Output: {\"processName\":\"Approve Development Goal: Goal Share Action\",\"action\":\"enable bypass\",\"isAsyncThere\":false}\n\n• Input: \"Enable bypass for Change Personal Information: Email Details\"\n• Output: {\"processName\":\"Change Personal Information: Email Details\",\"action\":\"enable bypass\",\"isAsyncThere\":false}\n\n\nMultiple processes example - \n• Input: “Set bypass for Promote, Hire” \n• Output: “Please specify only one process name for bypass status update.”\n\n\nReturn the identified processName as string, action as string and isAsyncThere as boolean value."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"ProcessNameActionAsync\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"processName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"action\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"isAsyncThere\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"processName\", \"action\", \"isAsyncThere\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check Process Name"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1763970323830",
            "false": "add_false_1763970263680"
          },
          "code": "CHECK_PROCESS_NAME",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
